Chapter: Pr2001Text
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Narrowing probe for the CDX2001 loss. `probe-pr87-alias` and
 `probe-pr87-direct` both show bare metal reporting CDX2001 "Integer vs
 Fun" where our zig-built compiler reports nothing. This asks whether the
 whole diagnostic is gone or only that shape: a Text where an Integer is
 declared is CDX2001 by a completely different route -- no function
 types, no arity, no self-reference.

 PREDICTION: bare metal refuses with CDX2001. If OUR ARM also refuses,
 the loss is specific to the Fun comparison and the hunt is narrow. If
 our arm accepts this too, CDX2001 is not being reported at all and the
 hunt is at the reporting site rather than the comparison.

Section: Functions

  m : Integer
  m = "not an integer"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show m)
  end
